data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":260,"item_id":"msg_3225ab8aa20d4cdb92b2848b929ef5aa","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"**Practical Guide to Tending a Small Vegetable Garden Through Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter**\n\nStarting a small vegetable garden in the spring, summer, autumn, and winter is a great way to grow food and enjoy fresh produce. Each season has its own unique challenges and opportunities. Below is a detailed guide to tending a small garden through these seasons, including an introduction and specific advice for each season.\n\n---\n\n### **Introduction**\n\nStarting a small vegetable garden is a great way to grow food, connect with nature, and enjoy the beauty of growing plants. Each season brings different weather, soil conditions, and plant needs. By following these seasonal tips, you can ensure a successful and healthy garden throughout the year.\n\n---\n\n### **Spring: Starting the Garden**\n\n**What to Do:**\n\n1. **Planting**  \n   - Choose a variety of vegetables that thrives in spring. Consider growing a mix of leafy greens (e.g., spinach, lettuce) and some more robust ones (e.g., tomatoes, peppers, carrots).  \n   - Ensure the soil is well-drained and rich in organic matter.  \n   - Plant in a sunny spot (sunlight is crucial for growth).  \n\n2. **Soil Preparation**  \n   - Before planting,","logprobs":[]}

