data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":260,"item_id":"msg_b784c7de699940cabbed0325eff174bc","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"# Practical Guide to Tending a Small Vegetable Garden Through Spring to Winter\n\n## Introduction\n\nStarting a small vegetable garden in the spring through winter is a rewarding and sustainable way to grow food in your own backyard. Each season offers unique challenges and opportunities, and with careful planning and consistent care, you can thrive in every part of the year.\n\nThis guide provides a detailed practical guide to tending a small vegetable garden through spring, summer, autumn, and winter. It includes specific advice for each season, helping you keep your garden healthy and productive throughout the growing season.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Spring: Starting the Garden\n\n**What to Do:**\n\n1. **Plant Seeds and Start Seeds**\n   - Choose a variety of small vegetables that you can grow in a small space. Consider your space and the climate. For example, if you live in a region with cold winters, you might start with a mix of leafy greens and root vegetables.\n   - Plant your seeds in well-drained soil. Ensure the soil is rich in organic matter to promote healthy growth.\n\n2. **Provide Nutrient-rich Soil**\n   - Before planting, amend the soil with compost or organic fertilizer to improve its fertility. This will help your vegetables grow stronger and more robust.\n\n3. **Plant","logprobs":[]}

