data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":260,"item_id":"msg_2a43a3d013f4484098a2f6b18392be12","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"# Practical Guide to Tending a Small Vegetable Garden Through Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter\n\n## Introduction\n\nStarting a small vegetable garden in the spring, summer, autumn, and winter is a great way to grow food and enjoy fresh produce right from your kitchen. Each season has its own unique challenges and opportunities. This guide will walk you through each season with practical advice and tips to help you thrive in every part of the growing season.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Spring: Starting the Garden\n\n**What to Do:**\n\n1. **Start Seeds Early**  \n   Begin planting in early spring (around March to April) to give your garden a head start. Choose a variety of vegetables that you can grow in your home. For example, tomatoes, zucchini, or peppers.\n\n2. **Planting Techniques**  \n   - Plant the seeds in well-drained soil.  \n   - Space the plants about 10–15 cm apart to allow proper growth.  \n   - Use a pot or a large container to plant in spring.  \n   - Water the soil regularly, especially in the first few weeks.\n\n3. **Fertilizing**  \n   - Before planting, apply a balanced fertilizer (like a 10–10–10","logprobs":[]}

