data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":260,"item_id":"msg_6dd4d82c86f940d4872fb3e8b8c70f52","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"# Practical Guide to Tending a Small Vegetable Garden Through Spring to Winter\n\n## Introduction\n\nStarting a small vegetable garden in the spring through winter is a rewarding and sustainable way to grow food in your own backyard. Each season offers unique challenges and opportunities, and with careful planning and consistent care, you can thrive in every part of the year.\n\nThis guide provides a detailed practical guide to tending a small vegetable garden through spring, summer, autumn, and winter. It includes specific advice for each season, helping you keep your garden healthy and productive throughout the growing season.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Spring: Starting the Garden\n\n**What to Do:**\n\n1. **Plant Seeds and Start Seeds**\n   - Choose a variety of small vegetables that you can grow in a pot or in your own garden. Consider your space and the type of soil you have.\n   - Start with a small pot (10–15 gallons) to avoid overwatering. Use a potting mix that is rich in organic matter.\n\n2. **Planting Seeds**\n   - Plant the seeds in well-drained soil. Ensure the soil is moist and not compacted.\n   - Plant the seeds in a pot or in the garden. Water the soil regularly to keep it moist.\n\n3.","logprobs":[]}

